This `concat` polyfill is installed as `Array.prototype.myConcat`. For which call does it behave differently from the built-in `concat`?

```js
function myConcat(...args) {
  const out = [...this];
  for (const a of args) {
    if (typeof a === 'object') out.push(...a);
    else out.push(a);
  }
  return out;
}
```

`fetchPage(cursor)` resolves to `{ items, nextCursor }`, and `nextCursor` is `null` on the last page. The API has three pages. What happens when `fetchAll()` runs?

```js
async function fetchAll() {
  const all = [];
  let cursor = null;
  while (true) {
    const { items, nextCursor } = await fetchPage(cursor);
    all.push(...items);
    if (!nextCursor) break;
  }
  return all;
}
```

Pages hold 10 items each and there are 10 pages. The consumer stops after it has 25 items. How many times is `getPage` called?

```js
async function* allItems() {
  let page = 0;
  let hasMore = true;
  while (hasMore) {
    const res = await getPage(page++);
    hasMore = res.hasMore;
    yield* res.items;
  }
}

const got = [];
for await (const item of allItems()) {
  got.push(item);
  if (got.length === 25) break;
}
```

This ES module binds `state.name` to a text input. The input's `input` listener runs `state.name = input.value`. What happens when that assignment runs?

```js
const input = document.querySelector('#name');
const state = new Proxy({ name: '' }, {
  set(target, key, value) {
    target[key] = value;
    if (key === 'name') input.value = value;
  },
});
input.addEventListener('input', () => { state.name = input.value; });
```

A fixed-height virtual list computes which rows to render. What does `range(1010)` return?

```js
const rowHeight = 40, viewport = 400, overscan = 2, total = 10000;

function range(scrollTop) {
  const first = Math.floor(scrollTop / rowHeight);
  const count = Math.ceil(viewport / rowHeight);
  const start = Math.max(0, first - overscan);
  const end = Math.min(total, first + count + overscan);
  return [start, end, start * rowHeight];
}
```

